    "body": "## Summary\n- let a reporter withdraw only their own still-pending job report\n- preserve the record as `WITHDRAWN` with an auditable `withdrawnAt` timestamp instead of deleting moderation history\n- add Flyway V30 constraints for the new state and timestamp consistency\n- expose the withdrawal action and timestamp on `/my-reports`\n- explicitly restrict admin moderation decisions to `REVIEWED` or `DISMISSED`\n- add backend regression coverage and update trust/safety documentation\n\n## Safety / privacy\n- lookup is scoped by both report id and authenticated reporter id, so the endpoint does not expose another user's report\n- reports cannot be withdrawn after moderation has started or completed\n- administrators cannot manufacture the reporter-only `WITHDRAWN` state\n- no moderator identity, internal moderation note, enforcement audit, location, route, tracking or payment data is exposed to reporters\n- withdrawn reports remain private history records and are no longer part of the default pending moderation queue\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend lint/build, Flyway/container runtime checks and existing smoke workflows. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
